    "title": "Tea Around the World",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "After water, tea is the most popular drink in the world. People first drank tea in China about five thousand years ago. Today, every country has its own way of making and drinking it."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "In Britain, people usually drink black tea with milk. Many add a spoonful of sugar. Afternoon tea is a famous tradition: at four o'clock, people drink tea with small sandwiches and cakes. In India, tea is often made with milk, sugar and spices such as ginger and cardamom. This drink is called chai, and street sellers make it in small pots."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "In Morocco, people drink green tea with fresh mint and a lot of sugar. They pour it from a high place into small glasses, which makes bubbles on top. Drinking this tea is a sign of friendship, and the host always offers it to guests. In Japan, tea is more formal. In a tea ceremony, a person prepares a special green tea slowly, and the guests drink it in silence."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Tea is also good for your health. It contains a little less caffeine than coffee and can help you feel calm. Many people think that green tea is the healthiest. However, tea can stain your teeth, and you should not drink it too hot. Which type do you prefer?"
      }
    ]
  },
